200 GeV. They observed strong suppression of high \(p_{T}\) hadron yields. ALICE also measured the nuclear modification factor \(R_{AA}\) for charged hadrons in central Pb-Pb collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}\) = 2.76 TeV [65] and compared the results to those of STAR and PHENIX in figure 1.11 According to the results, \(R_{AA}\) is less than unity. At \(p_{T}\) = 6-7 GeV/\(c\), a smaller drop in the \(R_{AA}\) value is seen for ALICE than for RHIC. When compared to RHIC, a strong suppression at LHC suggests that a lot of energy is lost at LHC. For high \(p_{T}\) (\(>\) 7GeV/\(c\)), a significant increase in \(R_{AA}\) is seen, which shows that high \(p_{T}\) hadrons lose a small amount of energy.

