##### 4.7.2.5 CME fraction (\(f_{CME}\))

Figure 4.26 displays the fraction of CME (\(f_{CME}\)) calculated using Eq. 4.7 versus \(n_{5}\)/s (the axial charge per entropy density) for Au+Au, Ru+Ru, and Zr+Zr collisions. The \(f_{CME}\) increases with an increase in externally injected CME signals, corresponding to an increase in axial charge per entropy density (\(n_{5}/s\)) from 0.0 to 0.2.

It is observed that for Au+Au collisions, \(f_{CME}\) increases from approximately 11.5% (\(n_{5}\)/\(s\)=0.0) to approximately 39% (\(n_{5}\)/\(s\)=0.2) considering top 20% \(f_{DbCS}\) as displayed in Fig. 4.26.

For Ru+Ru (Zr+Zr) collisions, \(f_{CME}\) increases from approximately 5% (3.6%) for \(n_{5}\)/\(s\)=0.0 to approximately 9.5% (9.4%) for \(n_{5}\)/\(s\)=0.2 for top 20% \(f_{DbCS}\). It is worth noting that for the \(n_{5}\)/\(s\)=0.0 case, \(f_{CME}\) exhibits positive values. The presence of 33% local charge conservation (LCC) in the samples with

