### 5.4 Non-Uniform Acceptance Correction

To account for the effects of detector acceptance, it is necessary to include corrections in the calculations of cumulants from multi-particle correlations. In detectors with uniform acceptance, certain terms in the calculations can be disregarded. However, for detectors that are "almost" perfect but still exhibit small deviations from perfect uniformity, it is important to reintroduce the terms that were previously eliminated [18][21]. The expressions for obtaining the acceptance correction in the calculations are as follows:

